@startuml answer_flow
' Odoo 16 - how the AI Assistant answers one question:
' Ask AI: ai.assistant.exchange.ask_ai -> _ask_ai_enqueue -> queue job _ask_ai_answer;
' app: ai.conversation.app_ask -> _app_enqueue -> queue job _app_answer;
' new answer: ai.assistant.exchange.action_send_new_answer -> either job, as the asker;
' all -> ai.assistant.engine._answer -> ai.claude.gateway._claude_chain
' (tool loop, ai_claude) -> ai.assistant.tools._execute per tool call
' -> _ask_ai_finish / _app_finish through _in_own_cursor;
' a refusal -> _close_unanswered through _close_in_own_cursor.
' Preview: Alt+D (PlantUML extension)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

title One question: queue job -> Claude tool loop -> answer

start

if (Ask AI?) then (yes)
  :check: AI Assistant group, a record with a chatter,
  not a Discuss channel nor an ai.* record,
  readable by the employee, not on the AI deny list;
  :the record's AI conversation, one for every asker,
  created with its first question;
  note right
    A first question that loses the conversation to a
    concurrent one is posted in a new transaction,
    which sees the winner's conversation.
  end note
  :question posted at once as an internal note
  by the employee, subtype Ask AI (notifies nobody);
else (app)
  :question added to the employee's conversation,
  which keeps the screen it was asked from;
endif
:ai.assistant.exchange row, pending, with the
companies selected when it was asked;
note right
  Send new answer (administrator, on an answer with a
  thumbs-down, not covered or not answered): a new row
  replying to it, same question, record or conversation,
  in the question's companies the asker still has; the
  answer, if to review, marked Fixed. Refused while a new
  answer to the question is pending, or when the asker
  could not ask it again.
end note
:queue job on root.ai_assistant
(one per question; a new answer's runs as the asker);

partition "queue job" {
  if (checks again: group;\nfor Ask AI the record) then (refused)
    :closed as Unavailable and refused,
    in a short transaction of its own,
    without asking Claude;
    if (new answer?) then (yes)
      :nothing posted, nobody told;
    elseif (Ask AI?) then (yes)
      :nothing on the record; a notification
      to the asker alone, quoting the question;
    else (app)
      :bus message carrying the refusal,
      shown in place of the answer;
    endif
    stop
  else (allowed)
  endif
  :system prompt + history (last 10 answered questions
  before the question, each with its latest answer)
  + context block (employee, now, companies,
  record or screen) + question;
  :_claude_chain: claude_models in order;
  repeat
    :Claude call (system prompt, tools and latest
    tool results marked for prompt caching);
    if (tool use?) then (yes)
      :each tool runs as the employee, in a savepoint
      rolled back, under tool_seconds; logged in
      ai.assistant.tool.call without the data read;
      note right
        Rights, record rules, companies, field groups,
        then the AI deny list.
        Errors are results the model reads.
      end note
    else (no)
    endif
  repeat while (tool use, within claude_max_tool_rounds\nand claude_tool_budget_seconds?) is (yes)
  -> no;
  note right
    tool_limit: no later model is asked.
    No answer from this model (refusal, empty, cut,
    unavailable...): the next model starts over.
  end note
}

partition "short transaction of its own" {
  if (still pending?) then (yes)
    if (answered?) then (yes)
      :state Answered, Not covered flag,
      model, tokens, cost, attempts;
    else (no)
      :state Unavailable: tool limit
      ("narrow it") or no Claude answer;
    endif
    if (Ask AI?) then (yes)
      :answer note by AI Assistant, subtype Ask AI,
      in reply to the question note, opening with
      a line quoting the asker and the question;
    else (app)
      :bus message carrying the answer
      to the asker's app or panel;
    endif
    if (new answer, answered?) then (yes)
      :asker alone notified (Inbox or email): Ask AI
      by the answer note, the app by a note on the
      AI conversation linking to the app;
    else (no)
    endif
    :deviations noted on the AI conversation;
  else (no)
    :nothing: answered or closed meanwhile;
  endif
}
note right
  Tried 3 times on concurrent updates; then one
  more transaction closes the question as
  Unavailable and tells the asker, without a
  second Claude call. A conflict there too
  leaves it pending for the cron.
end note

stop

legend right
  A job that fails or is cancelled closes its question at once.
  The cron (every 5 minutes) closes questions still pending
  pending_stale_seconds after their job started or was enqueued.
  An app asker who lost the AI Assistant since gets the refusal.
endlegend
@enduml
